  "name": "EDTA protonation (H₄Y with NaOH)",
  "description": "The free acid H₄Y (pKa 2.00, 2.69, 6.13, 10.37) with 0.1000 M NaOH. The first two protons are lost together (pKa values only 0.7 apart), then one at pH 6.1 and the last at 10.4: this is why EDTA titrations need a buffer. The species Y⁴⁻, which binds metals, is only 30 % of the EDTA at pH 10.",
